# {{feature_id}} · Design and implementation

Use the sections needed to explain this Feature under `methodology/02-feature-list-schema.md`. This is an optional outline, not a requirement to create a file or fill every heading. Render prose in `document_language`.

## Goal and boundaries

Link the owning Product, Feature JSON and relevant AC. Explain the technical question and scope without copying requirements.

## Existing behavior and constraints

Describe the relevant implementation and limitations. For each material constraint, explain what it protects and how it applies here; use relative links to project rules, applicable `agent-rules`, architecture and ADRs. Distinguish confirmed facts from assumptions and identify versions for sensitive external references.

## Proposed design

Explain responsibilities, interfaces, dependency directions and authoritative state ownership. Record local choices and reasons; link important cross-Feature tradeoffs to their ADR. Clearly identify unresolved choices.

## Runtime and failure flows

Trace the useful triggers, ordering, state changes, lifecycle boundaries, failures and recovery. Use a diagram only where it clarifies the flow.

## Implementation and verification reasoning

Describe meaningful implementation dependencies and why the existing verification plan covers the relevant risks. Keep executable test mappings and obligations in Feature JSON/Registry, and link original results rather than copying a second plan or result table.

## Actual outcome and deviations

Before final verification, reconcile the design with what was implemented. Preserve material reasons for an approved change of plan, link current subsystem documentation, and state remaining limitations. Feature status and current blockers remain in their existing records.
